# Deploy via preview branches, not straight to main

`main` is this project's production branch — every push to it deploys
straight to the live site at epilepsysucks.org with no review step. Don't
push directly to `main` for feature/content/layout work.

For every change (unless the user explicitly says to push straight to
production):

1. `git checkout -b <short-descriptive-branch-name>` off latest `main`.
2. Make the change, test locally, commit.
3. `git push -u origin <branch-name>`.
4. `gh pr create` — this triggers a Vercel **Preview** deployment (not
   Production) tied to the branch.
5. Get the preview URL (`vercel ls`, `gh pr checks`, or the Vercel bot
   comment on the PR) and share it with the user so they can review the
   live preview before it ships.
6. Only after the user approves: merge the PR into `main` (e.g.
   `gh pr merge --squash --delete-branch`), which triggers the Production
   deploy.

If the user asks for a quick one-off fix and explicitly says to skip the
PR/preview step, it's fine to push straight to `main` — but default to the
branch + PR + preview flow otherwise.
